WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:02.306
Two in the morning, in Dhaka.

00:02.306 --> 00:05.189
Her tin roof is still giving back the day’s heat.

00:05.189 --> 00:08.130
She’s barely slept, and her shift starts at seven.

00:09.450 --> 00:13.807
Extreme heat is a global health emergency. And it’s a wicked problem.

00:13.807 --> 00:17.470
Every link runs through someone’s health, income, or home.

00:18.950 --> 00:23.846
We mapped ten systems, seventy-four consequences, and eighteen vicious cycles.

00:23.846 --> 00:29.620
We also found twenty-six places to break them, and fourteen institutions holding the levers.

00:30.950 --> 00:33.580
One heatwave hits ten systems at once.

00:33.580 --> 00:37.387
Land, water, energy, cities, bodies, wages and budgets.

00:37.387 --> 00:41.470
Each one pushes on the others, and the red links loop back.

00:42.950 --> 00:46.576
Take one of those eighteen cycles: the poverty-heat trap.

00:46.576 --> 00:50.775
A worker who can’t afford to stop falls ill. Illness costs income.

00:50.775 --> 00:53.510
And lost income makes stopping even harder.

00:54.950 --> 00:57.761
Why wicked? There’s no single cause to fix.

00:57.761 --> 01:01.749
Every solution changes the problem. The problem feeds itself.

01:01.749 --> 01:05.280
And it lands unequally. Same heatwave, different fate.

01:06.450 --> 01:08.651
Some points sit where many loops meet.

01:08.651 --> 01:12.300
Protect people from heatstroke, and five cycles weaken at once.

01:15.450 --> 01:19.127
Yet six loops have nobody on our list working to break them.

01:19.127 --> 01:22.620
Meanwhile, twenty-five organisations crowd onto just one.

01:23.950 --> 01:26.386
Every loop runs through an institution.

01:26.386 --> 01:28.946
No single institution can break them all.

01:28.946 --> 01:30.820
The response has to be shared.

01:31.950 --> 01:35.706
Pull one thread, and the whole web moves.

01:35.706 --> 01:38.480
Let’s find the loops your institution can break.
